meta {
  name: Get Deal Audit Review
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/deal-audits/deals/{{auditDealId}}/review
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{auditReviewerToken}}
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

script:post-response {
  // The item the verdict requests rule on, and a policy for Policies ›
  // Download New Business Application. Runtime-only vars.
  if (res.getStatus() === 200) {
    const body = res.getBody();
    if (body.items.length > 0) {
      bru.setVar("reviewItemId", body.items[0].id);
    }
    if (body.policies.length > 0) {
      bru.setVar("reviewPolicyId", body.policies[0].id);
    }
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("returns the audit, the deal and every section of the page", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.audit.dealId).to.equal(bru.getVar("auditDealId"));
    expect(body.deal.id).to.equal(bru.getVar("auditDealId"));
    expect(body.policies).to.be.an("array");
    expect(body).to.have.property("quoteRecap");
    expect(body).to.have.property("lead");
    expect(body.items).to.be.an("array").and.not.be.empty;
  });

  test("the manager sees every item, manager-only ones included", function () {
    // The producer's board would show only the producerVisible ones.
    for (const item of res.getBody().items) {
      expect(item.producerVisible).to.be.a("boolean");
      expect(item.requiresUpload).to.be.a("boolean");
      expect(item).to.have.property("review");
    }
  });

  test("the tally and the approve gate agree", function () {
    const { audit, items } = res.getBody();
    const passed = items.filter((item) => item.review.verdict === "pass");
    expect(audit.counts.passed).to.equal(passed.length);
    expect(audit.unmet.length).to.equal(items.length - passed.length);
    expect(audit.canApprove).to.equal(audit.canReview && audit.unmet.length === 0);
  });

  test("the producer just submitted it, so the manager may review", function () {
    const audit = res.getBody().audit;
    expect(audit.auditStatus).to.equal("Pending");
    expect(audit.canReview).to.equal(true);
  });

  test("documents carry metadata, never a storage key", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    const raw = JSON.stringify(body);
    expect(raw).to.not.match(/agencies\/[0-9a-f]{24}\//);
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /deal-audits/deals/:dealId/review — the Deal Audit page (PAC-106)

  Everything the manager's Deal Audit page renders, in one request: the
  workflow, the sale, the policies it bound (with their new business
  applications), the quote it came from, the lead, and **every** checklist
  item — manager-only ones included.

  - **Module:** `deal_audits`
  - **Permission:** `deal_audits:read` **and** `management:read`.
  - **Data scope:** the audit must be in the caller's reach (branch / agency /
    assignee-or-reviewer under `own`); else `404`.

  Readable in any status. The page's actions are live only while
  `audit.canReview` — `Pending`, and not the caller's own submission.

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  {
    "audit": {
      "id": "665f...9c1",
      "dealId": "665f...a03",
      "auditStatus": "Pending",
      "assignee": { "type": "user", "id": "665f...b11", "name": "Pat Producer" },
      "reviewer": { "type": "user", "id": "665f...b12", "name": "Morgan Manager" },
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-15T14:20:00.000Z",
      "sentBack": null,
      "canSubmit": false,
      "canReview": true,
      "canApprove": false,
      "canSendBack": false,
      "unmet": [{ "id": "665f...ac1", "itemName": "Good Student" }],
      "counts": { "passed": 6, "failed": 0, "remaining": 1 }
    },
    "deal": {
      "id": "665f...a03",
      "clientName": "Jane Homeowner",
      "householdId": "665f...b20",
      "householdName": "Homeowner Household",
      "leadId": "665f...c30",
      "soldDate": "2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z",
      "soldDay": "2026-10-09",
      "dealType": "Auto",
      "policyTypes": ["Auto"],
      "premium": 1450,
      "producerId": "665f...b11",
      "producerName": "Pat Producer",
      "businessDaysOpen": 6,
      "aging": true
    },
    "policies": [
      {
        "id": "665f...d40",
        "policyNumber": "804 123 456",
        "policyType": "Auto",
        "carrier": "Allstate",
        "premium": 1450,
        "effectiveDate": "2026-10-10",
        "newBusinessApplication": {
          "filename": "application.pdf",
          "contentType": "application/pdf",
          "size": 2048,
          "uploadedAt": "2026-10-09T17:05:00.000Z"
        }
      }
    ],
    "quoteRecap": {
      "id": "665f...e50",
      "quoteDate": "2026-10-06T15:00:00.000Z",
      "premium": 1450,
      "itemCount": 2,
      "productsQuoted": ["Auto"],
      "policies": [{ "policyType": "Auto", "premium": 1450, "itemCount": 2 }],
      "notes": "Two cars, one teen driver.",
      "producerName": "Pat Producer",
      "document": { "filename": "quote.pdf", "contentType": "application/pdf", "size": 4096, "uploadedAt": null }
    },
    "lead": {
      "id": "665f...c30",
      "name": "Jane Homeowner",
      "status": "Sold",
      "temperature": "Hot",
      "leadSourceName": "Mailer",
      "createdDate": "2026-10-01T15:00:00.000Z",
      "producerName": "Pat Producer",
      "phone": "5125550100",
      "email": "jane@example.com"
    },
    "items": [
      {
        "id": "665f...ac1",
        "itemName": "Good Student",
        "category": "Auto",
        "subjectName": null,
        "producerVisible": true,
        "requiresUpload": true,
        "open": false,
        "isResolved": true,
        "resolvedAt": "2026-10-14T10:00:00.000Z",
        "producerNote": "Transcript attached.",
        "attachments": [
          { "index": 0, "filename": "transcript.pdf", "contentType": "application/pdf", "size": 30720, "uploadedAt": "2026-10-14T10:00:00.000Z" }
        ],
        "review": { "verdict": null, "note": null, "reviewedAt": null, "reviewedByName": null }
      }
    ]
  }
  ```

  - **Two truths per item**: the producer's claim (`isResolved`,
    `producerNote`, `attachments`) and the manager's verification
    (`review.verdict` / `review.note`). The Approve gate reads only the
    verdict.
  - `unmet` lists every item whose verdict is not `pass`; `canApprove` is
    `canReview && unmet is empty`; `canSendBack` is `canReview && counts.failed > 0`.
  - `quoteRecap` is the recap the deal names (`quoteRecapId`), else the
    lead's most recent recap on or before the sold day — `null` when there is
    none. Its document opens through **Download Quote Recap Document**.
  - A policy's `newBusinessApplication` is metadata only; the file opens
    through **Policies › Download New Business Application**. `null` when none
    was uploaded (every migrated policy).
  - `lead.phone` / `lead.email` come from the lead's primary contact (else the
    household's).
  - `items` sort by category (Common, Prior Insurance, Auto, Home, Landlord),
    then name.

  ## Errors
  - `401 Unauthorized` — missing/expired token.
  - `403 Forbidden` — missing `deal_audits:read` or `management:read`.
  - `404 Not Found` — no audit for that deal, or out of the caller's reach.
}
